WEBVTT

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:13.160
It was like she was a tiger...

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.600
Strong and vibrant...

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.230
That was how we met!

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.830
Man, doing chorus all morning really sucks...

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.730
I don't know why it's so long.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.700
Like, for sure!

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:21.970
Something the matter?

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.430
Did you forget something?

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.200
Um... Yes.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.870
Then we'll go on ahead, okay?

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.980
I wonder why I can't handle things like everyone else.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:56.030
Sorry I'm late, everyone!  I'm just a big dummyhead, aren't I?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.140
I'm sorry, everyone!  Wait here, I'll be back in a dash!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:05.900
It's no good.  I'm in high school now, but nothing's changed.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.830
Well, yeah... People can't change that easily, I guess.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.310
I'm lost...

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.430
I actually got lost.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.670
And just after I started here.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.630
This school is way too big!

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:45.820
The private school, Kamizono Academy.  Established in '56.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.480
If you combine the elementary, middle, and high schools,

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.790
it has a student population of more than 3,000.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.130
It's the same place again.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.090
I passed through here before.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.100
"To inspire talent in all directions, no matter what the field!" is the school's motto.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.910
Ah, what am I saying?

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:22.530
And here I am, right back in the same place again.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.640
What am I gonna do?

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.740
"A new student has gone missing while changing classes"

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:28.910
It's so embarrassing!

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.940
I can't go on living like this!

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.170
A-A person!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.840
U-Um, excuse me!

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.880
Yes?  What is it?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.330
Yes!  Um... Well, you see...

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.680
Could you tell me how to get...

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.300
Huh?

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:56.850
My, have I not seen you somewhere prior to this?

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:02.500
Yes.  I'm pretty sure we're in the same class.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.320
I'm Nonomura Ayumi.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.070
The "no" is written with the character for "ability."

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.080
Iizuka Tatsuki.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.330
The first "I" as in "Itou Hirobumi," the second as in "Inoue Kaoru."

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:20.250
Political families...

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.550
The "zuka" as in "Takarazuka," and the "ryou" character from "Sakamoto Ryouma" plus "hime."

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.100
Noromura-san, was it?

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.040
It's Nonomura!

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.820
If you were heading from the music room back to the classroom, why are you here?

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.480
Well, it's because I think I'm los...

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.250
Yes?

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.210
I could not hear you very well.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.610
It looks like I'm lost.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.410
"Two new students have gone missing while changing classes."

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.160
You don't have to make such a big deal...

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.660
Totally lost.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.360
This school is way too big!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.690
Is that so?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:00.180
Indeed, it is quite the ridiculously large campus.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.750
It is only natural for someone who is here for the first time to get lost.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.530
Although <b>I</b> have been attending here since elementary school.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.730
Really?

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.090
Thank goodness!  Then you can take me back to the classroom, right?

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:22.940
Iizuka-san!

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:30.090
What's wrong?  Did I just say something really bad?

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.410
Now that I think about it, what was she doing here anyway?

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.840
Class must have already started by now...

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.920
It couldn't be...

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.590
She's lying?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.850
I should probably ask her.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.460
But, how?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:01.090
Um, you're lost too, aren't you?

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:03.670
As if!  That's way too forward.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:06.780
If I was wrong, that'd be super rude!

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:13.660
But, at this rate, we'll just keep going in circles.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.370
I just have to put one foot forward, and have the courage...

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:20.890
The courage!

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.200
Um...

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:24.690
What is it?

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.710
Oh, nothing...

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.180
She knew what I was gonna say!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.000
She totally knew!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.810
There's no way she'd have turned and said that so quickly unless she knew.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:41.210
Her back is totally screaming "Don't talk to me!"

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:45.320
No matter what I say to her now, she's not going to respond favorably.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.740
But, is that really true?

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:52.740
Wouldn't it actually make it easier for Iizuka-san to tell me the truth?

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:57.740
Isn't it the fundamental of good communication to consider the standpoint of the other person?

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:58.710
Um!

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.320
What is it?!

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.250
The next class has started already, hasn't it?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.800
And your point?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.670
You can do this, Ayumi!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.190
Could it be that you also don't know where...

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.920
Did I not say that I have attended this academy since elementary school?

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.440
Six years in elementary school and three in middle school.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.290
This is my tenth year here, you know.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.110
I-I'm sorry...

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:33.680
And yet I am still unable to gain a complete grasp of the entire school.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.110
Iizuka-san...

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:42.870
We shall continue on wandering around the school like this.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:43.710
You're not serious...

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:46.940
This academy has a large number of legends, you know.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.790
From the standards, like the door that cannot be opened,

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:52.020
the disappearing transfer student, the forbidden laboratory...

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.860
Urban legends?

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.730
We have fallen into an infinite corridor!

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.380
It can't be!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.180
Or not.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.310
You believed me?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.850
It was a lie?

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.480
You are like some endangered species, are you not?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.210
You were lying?  Thank goodness!

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.280
It does not change the fact that we do not know the location of the classroom, you know.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.280
So you <i>are</i> lost?

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.710
What a gust of wind!

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.590
I-It's broken!  Broken!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.440
W-What?

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.920
What is it?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:26.180
Ow!  Ow, it hurts!  It hurts!

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.180
Um... Oh, right!  An ambulance!

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.540
What?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.190
There is no need for that, is there?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.140
Iizuka-san?

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:32.650
I said it hurts!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:39.110
Ah, the <i>pain</i>!  The pain!  The pain!

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:36.110
Oh?  You have a cell phone?

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.110
Yeah.  I'll call an ambulance now, okay?

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.070
Ah, mind your heads.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:41.950
Eh?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:42.780
Huh?

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.160
Our heads?

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.860
W-W-What?!

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:01.340
Huh?  The pain's gone for some reason.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:05.140
It was nothing, just as I figured.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.460
But it totally hurt like just before.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:08.440
Torako.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:13.530
Oh, right.  You really got a good memory there, Suzu.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:14.420
Laters.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:17.410
Hold on you two!

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.510
Wait, me too!

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.950
What the heck?!

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.830
What in heaven were you thinking?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.960
I couldn't believe my eyes that someone would suddenly jump from the second story window.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.210
True...

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:36.610
But it kind of seems like an incredible way to meet someone.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:40.420
I have no idea how you came up with that interpretation.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.770
I'm Kageyama Torako.

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:45.120
Kageyama is written with the characters for "up", "down", and "mountain."

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.890
And she's Saotome Suzume.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.200
Suzu.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.600
She says to call her "Suzu."

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.120
I'm Nonomura Ayumi.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:53.940
How 'bout you?

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.330
Iizuka Tatsuki.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:58.080
The first "I" as in "Itou Hirobumi"-

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:02.630
We had some, uh, circumstances, so this is actually the first day the two of us came to school.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:03.590
Circumstances?

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:04.950
Is that so?

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:11.380
And after we said "hi" to this principal lookin' person, we were tryin' to head straight back to our classroom,

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:14.420
but this school's bigger than big...

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:15.790
Yeah.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:16.620
Ain't it!

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.470
It's really big.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:21.190
We got like super-totally lost!

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:26.430
Then, we saw that building called the "classroom wing" or something from the window.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:34.520
But, as we went down the floors, we lost our sense of direction more and more.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.420
We had a serious case of "lost child syndrome."

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:39.970
And that's when it hit me!

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:44.650
I thought, "why not head straight towards our goal from right there?"

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.730
And that is...

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.560
That is why you jumped out from the window?

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:54.090
Ah, yeah... Guess it was the second floor, yeah...

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.040
I cannot believe this!

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.340
No way but forward!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:05.340
True, we might be able to make it through just by going in that direction...

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:17.850
A fence.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:23.860
SIGNS:  Don't come in this way! -- Gardening Club
Don't pick the bluebells!! -- Academy Director

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:20.880
No way but forward!

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.720
Can we go through here?

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.860
The gardening club?

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:27.000
Suzu, are we going in the right direction?

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:30.830
We are.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.410
Is it really okay for us to be going through here?

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:36.290
This has really become quite preposterous.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.210
No way but forward!

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.510
Suzu?

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.500
Onward!  Onward!

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:56.850
Come again!

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.870
Pardon us.

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.480
Who are you people?

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:11.700
The high school is over there!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.050
I'm sorry, we're just a little lost...

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.950
Pardon us.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.070
This academy really is big.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.550
That way!  Course correction!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:35.550
Do you not think that it would have been better to have asked that teacher how to get to the classroom wing?

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:36.840
Oh, we could have.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:37.980
But we're almost there.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.400
We are?

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.080
Probably.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:43.110
It'll be fine, I tell you!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:47.690
Um, I don't think we've actually been going straight the whole time.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:48.640
Really?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.950
Please stop for a moment.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.050
What?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.960
Everyone, are you right or left handed?

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:03.500
Huh?

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:06.020
I am left handed.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:07.860
I'm right handed.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:09.970
Me, too.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:14.770
Then there is no way we could move in a straight line.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:20.650
With three right handed people and only one left handed person, it's natural to constantly curve to the right.

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:25.270
Unless there are an equal number of left and right handed people, a group cannot move in a straight line.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.060
Say what?

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:32.030
There is no point to just moving around randomly.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:36.910
Whether or not there's a point, I'm gonna go where I feel like!  That's the way I live my life.

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:41.230
Such illogical movements will do naught but waste one's precious time!

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:44.610
"Wasting precious time..."  What are you, like, 50?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.500
How dare you say such rude things to me!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.420
Especially after you getting everyone mixed up in your selfish thoughtless actions...

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.800
You damned egotist!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.470
What did you say, you bobbed-head?!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.590
What was that?  What did you just say?

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:56.140
W-What?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.140
I think I have GPS on here.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.560
GPS?

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:03.450
Global Positioning System.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:04.650
What's that?

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:10.570
They explained that it can tell you where you are on the school grounds or something on the first day.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.280
High-tech, isn't it?

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.490
They really said something like that?

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:15.630
Yes!

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.510
There it is!

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.110
So they gave that kind of orientation?

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:23.790
Well, this is quite the accomplishment, Nonomura-san.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:27.710
Good goin', Ayu!

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:30.170
Ayu...

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:35.590
I was helpful to everyone!

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.310
Things <i>are</i> different than in middle school!

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:45.100
Registration fee?

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:48.770
But...

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.880
No way but forward!

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:54.480
That's the fastest way, after all!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.380
It's the thought that counts.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.250
However, Kageyama-san.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.150
Using my family name seems so stiff...

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.670
Call me by my first name!

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:09.250
In that case, Torako-san.

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:12.710
You did say "forward," if I recall.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.720
Um, it seems to be locked...

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.690
The classroom wing is further back, isn't it?

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.680
What shall we do?  Look for a way around?

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:36.780
Suzu... Try turning the knob.

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.720
Why did you ask her to...

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:45.280
Nothing really, she's just like some crazy Hercules.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:46.910
Hercules?

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.780
What?  Did it open?

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:52.540
It came off.

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.090
Then, so be it!

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:02.840
Stop this at once!  Is it really that important to keep going straight?

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.810
Let me go, let me go!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.420
Calm down and find a way around!

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:08.730
No way!  I hate detours!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:09.930
But to go so far as to...

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:12.450
There is <i>no way</i> I'm takin' a detour!

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:16.690
Give me that!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:36.070
If someone sees us now...

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.890
No way!

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:53.080
What in the world are you guys doing?!

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.750
What... a left...

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.270
All right, let's beat it outta here!

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.430
Um, but... that was...

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:29.080
Don't worry!  I don't think he saw our faces.

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.810
That's not what I meant.  This person is...

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.750
Don't sweat it, just follow me!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:48.290
Really... Who in the world is she?

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:59.710
Now then... Kageyama Torako.

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:10.680
Ka~ge~ya~ma~ To~ra~ko~

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.750
Yesh.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.320
Iizuka Tatsuki!

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.520
Yes.

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.710
Saotome Suzume.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.590
Nonomura Ayumi!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:32.580
You four... Get your butts to the teachers' office after class.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.210
SIGN:  Teachers' Office

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:40.510
Honestly, I don't care what the hell problems you have as new students or newcomers,

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.840
but to knock me out is just...

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.380
If this were a public school you guys would be expelled!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:49.740
But I hope you realize how lucky you are that this is a private academy, and I'm this nice a guy...

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:52.340
When you get angry, is it really okay just to hit something?

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:56.190
Ah, but I really want to hit something from the bottom of my heart right now, with all my feeling...

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.770
Guidance!

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:01.580
If you must then just imagine it in your mind and stop there.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:02.760
And anyway, lately,

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.960
the second I lay a hand on a female student I'd be labeled as one of those "corporal punishment" teachers,

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:07.110
could I really live with that?

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:10.470
And ever more and more these days lately people will put those who do that sort of thing into groups, it keeps escalating...

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:12.310
So, why is it if you raise a hand against a female student it's sexual harassment?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.330
It always becomes a big deal, "Sexual harassment!"

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.620
And it's BECAUSE we're in such troubling times that I dare...

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.210
That I dare to think, what is the right thing?  Is this okay?

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:19.560
When I think about it in my own head, I as a teacher... nay, I as a <i>man</i>...

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:23.580
In any case, never do something like that again!

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:41.110
Um, well...

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.100
Just count on me from now on!

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.540
Silence, you!

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:22.330
So, what's up next week on Hyakko?

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:23.940
"You can't catch a tiger's cub if you don't go into the tiger's den."

00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:24.810
What does that mean?

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:27.430
It means when you want something, you have to risk something to get it.

00:23:27.430 --> 00:23:28.340
Risk?

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:31.120
Hitsugi already appeared a little bit, but I wonder if anyone out there noticed?

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:32.810
"Find Hitsugi!" eh?

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:34.490
Look forward to next time!
